From c85bbf15995e2b5ae1c577342cddf555fc9e759e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:17:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 23/24] Believe 26.6.2's kernel in the wire watch, as 27.2's

The watch and guard checked their offsets against two 27.2 dumps and
turned themselves off on any other kernel. A 26.6.2 (25G83) panic dump
has the same layout on all 8 of its wired mappings: the 0x98-byte
MappingInternal with id at +0x30, size 0x200 at +0x40, +0x48 and +0x50
zero, the surface descriptor at +0x20, the page-table descriptor at
+0x58 and the page count at +0x80; the descriptors' _wireCount +0x88,
_initialized +0x8c, _length +0x50, mixed data +0x90 with its length at
+0x18, _pages +0x98 and _buffer +0xb8; and their class in the kernel's
__DATA_CONST. Its kernel differs only where the checks already allow:
VBAR_EL1 is 0x6000 into __TEXT_EXEC rather than at its start, and the
scan down from it meets a kext's header (filetype 0xb) 68 pages before
the kernel's, which the scan already passes over since it takes an
MH_EXECUTE only.

So 26.6.2's version string joins 27.2's, matched exactly as before
(KNOWN_KERNEL_VERSIONS). 13.6 and 14.6.1 lay the mapping out without the
Sonoma shift, and 15.6.1 has not been checked; they stay off.

Tests (lib, --test-threads=1): 2309 passed, 0 failed. New: a kext's
header between VBAR_EL1 and the kernel's is passed over, and alone is no
kernel; 26.6.2's string with VBAR 0x6000 into a two-page __TEXT_EXEC
and a kext header on the way is verified, its mapping watched and
condemned at the drop, while the 13.6, 14.6.1 and 15.6.1 strings are
refused. No guest was booted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
